 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nJSON IS validation parsing incorrect for WITHOUT UNIQUE KEYS\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen parsing JSON IS validation expressions with `WITHOUT UNIQUE KEYS`, the parser incorrectly sets the `_with` flag to `None` instead of `False`, causing incorrect behavior in JSON validation checks.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport sqlglot\n\n# This should parse correctly but doesn't\nsql = \"SELECT js IS JSON ARRAY WITHOUT UNIQUE KEYS FROM t\"\nparsed = sqlglot.parse_one(sql, dialect=\"postgres\")\nprint(parsed)\n\n# Expected behavior vs actual behavior\nsql2 = \"SELECT js IS JSON ARRAY WITH UNIQUE KEYS FROM t\" \nparsed2 = sqlglot.parse_one(sql2, dialect=\"postgres\")\nprint(parsed2)\n```\n\nThe issue occurs when parsing JSON validation expressions that use `WITHOUT UNIQUE KEYS` - the parser logic incorrectly handles the `WITHOUT` case, setting the internal `_with` variable to `None` when it should be `False` to properly distinguish between `WITH` and `WITHOUT` cases.\n</issue>\n",
